under the BSD 3-Clause License. They are fetched at build time rather than vendored; a binary built from this source
embeds them, so a redistributor of such a binary carries that notice with it.

FLUTE is due to C. C. N. Chu and Y.-C. Wong, "FLUTE: Fast Lookup Table Based Rectilinear Steiner
Minimal Tree Algorithm for VLSI Design" (IEEE TCAD, 2008). The wirelength/depth trade-off follows
C. J. Alpert et al., "Prim-Dijkstra Revisited" (ISPD 2018).
